From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastian Matkovich <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 22:29:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: dsi-cm: native backlight starts at full brightness

Without a backlight in the device tree (the Nokia N950), the panel's own
DCS brightness is registered as the backlight with brightness 0. Power on
sets the DCS brightness to 0xff, but the backlight_enable() that follows
writes the backlight device's brightness, 0, so the screen stays dark
until user space sets a brightness. Start it at the maximum, as the old
omapdss panel-taal driver did.

Untested on hardware.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-dsi-cm.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-dsi-cm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-dsi-cm.c
index d6a6b346c..990c990bb 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-dsi-cm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-dsi-cm.c
@@ -892,6 +892,7 @@ static int dsicm_probe(struct mipi_dsi_device *dsi)
 	if (ddata->use_dsi_backlight) {
 		struct backlight_properties props = { 0 };
 		props.max_brightness = 255;
+		props.brightness = 255;
 		props.type = BACKLIGHT_RAW;
 
 		bldev = devm_backlight_device_register(dev, dev_name(dev),
-- 
2.56.0

